WEBVTT

00:00:58.262 --> 00:01:01.641
or the unrecoverable collapse 
of human civilization—

00:01:01.641 --> 00:01:03.559
has steadily increased.

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:07.021
It’s well within our power
to reduce this risk,

00:01:07.021 --> 00:01:08.606
but in order to do so,

00:01:08.606 --> 00:01:11.359
we have to understand which 
of our activities

00:01:11.359 --> 00:01:15.863
pose existential threats now, 
and which might in the future.

00:01:16.489 --> 00:01:20.868
So far, our species has survived
2,000 centuries,

00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:24.622
each with some extinction risk
from natural causes—

00:01:24.622 --> 00:01:27.750
asteroid impacts, supervolcanoes,
and the like.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.338
Assessing existential risk is 
an inherently uncertain business